1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
It's a new white-living record!

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,000
You're so strong!

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,000
I'm not strong!

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,000
I'm not strong!

5
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,000
I'm not strong!

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
I'm not strong!

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
I'm not strong!

8
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,000
I'm not strong!

9
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
I'm not strong!

10
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
I'm not strong!

11
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,000
I'm not strong!

12
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,000
I'm not strong!

13
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,000
I'm not strong!

14
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,160
So strong!

15
00:00:30,719 --> 00:00:34,119
That's so light I could lift it up with my finger!

16
00:00:36,759 --> 00:00:40,039
Oh my! But do you think you could lift up your nightstand?

17
00:00:40,359 --> 00:00:42,120
Don't know. Never tried it.

18
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:43,600
So then go on!

19
00:00:48,039 --> 00:00:49,079
No way!

20
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:52,200
And you are so much bigger than that nightstand!

21
00:00:52,439 --> 00:00:56,280
But watch, I can lift this big pencil!

22
00:00:56,280 --> 00:01:00,320
And just look how much smaller I am!

23
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,359
So, who's stronger, you or me?

24
00:01:04,239 --> 00:01:05,799
Well, I guess it's not me.

25
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:11,680
The Fixies may be very small,

26
00:01:11,760 --> 00:01:14,960
but they are actually much stronger than humans!

27
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:16,480
Yes, it's true!

28
00:01:17,159 --> 00:01:18,400
What, you don't believe me?

29
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:21,120
Well, who's stronger, an elephant or an ant?

30
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:22,879
You think it's the elephant.

31
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:24,920
Well, of course, it's so much bigger!

32
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:29,799
But did you know that one ant can lift up 50 ants its own size?

33
00:01:29,799 --> 00:01:32,799
And an elephant? It can't even hold up one!

34
00:01:33,439 --> 00:01:37,680
So it turns out that for its size an ant is much stronger than an elephant.

35
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:39,920
And the same goes for Fixies.

36
00:01:40,159 --> 00:01:43,120
Fixies are incredibly strong for their size.

37
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:47,159
They can lift things that are a hundred times heavier than they are.

38
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:50,920
And Fixies can jump 50 times higher than their own height!

39
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,960
If humans were as strong as Fixies are,

40
00:01:53,959 --> 00:01:57,799
They'd be able to lift an automobile all by themselves!

41
00:02:00,839 --> 00:02:04,039
Yeah, Tom Thomas, it's time you built up your strength!

42
00:02:04,039 --> 00:02:04,839
Well, how?

43
00:02:04,839 --> 00:02:06,199
Start lifting dumbbells!

44
00:02:06,199 --> 00:02:09,159
Or if you want to, you can use my barbell.

45
00:02:10,599 --> 00:02:11,479
No, thanks.

46
00:02:11,479 --> 00:02:13,639
I'll use the dumbbells my dad has.

47
00:02:13,799 --> 00:02:15,479
They're in his office, I think.

48
00:02:18,039 --> 00:02:19,319
Oh, there's one!

49
00:02:20,599 --> 00:02:22,120
And where's the other one?

50
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:26,640
Aha! There you are! I'll get you out of there!

51
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:31,120
Come on, come on!

52
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:32,840
I'm helping you here!

53
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:34,840
It's stuck!

54
00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:35,920
Alright!

55
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:37,719
Move aside!

56
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:39,319
I'll get it right out!

57
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:44,680
What is this? Glue to the floor or something?

58
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:46,520
Hey!

59
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,400
What's all the racket?

60
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:50,600
Hi there, Simka!

61
00:02:50,879 --> 00:02:53,040
We can't get the dumbbell out from under there.

62
00:02:53,039 --> 00:02:56,519
Well, of course you can't. The sofa is pressing down on it.

63
00:02:56,639 --> 00:02:58,239
So that's what it is.

64
00:02:58,679 --> 00:03:01,319
And I was worried that I lost all my strength.

65
00:03:01,719 --> 00:03:04,599
Well, that means we have to lift up this sofa.

66
00:03:05,319 --> 00:03:07,799
We can't do that. It's too heavy for us.

67
00:03:07,919 --> 00:03:08,959
We can do it.

68
00:03:09,159 --> 00:03:12,359
Tom Thomas, get me your hockey stick from your room.

69
00:03:14,359 --> 00:03:17,519
We can't move a sofa with a hockey stick?

70
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:19,319
Don't worry, you'll see.

71
00:03:19,319 --> 00:03:23,519
Here, I've brought it.

72
00:03:23,799 --> 00:03:24,879
What is it for?

73
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:27,400
We're going to use it as a lever.

74
00:03:27,519 --> 00:03:28,439
A lever?

75
00:03:28,639 --> 00:03:29,719
Well, yeah!

76
00:03:33,199 --> 00:03:36,000
A lever works the same way that a seesaw does

77
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:39,319
with a board resting on top of a piece called the fulcrum.

78
00:03:39,439 --> 00:03:42,120
But with a lever one side is longer than the other.

79
00:03:42,199 --> 00:03:44,560
And that's the secret to its power!

80
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:48,439
With a lever's help it's possible to lift any weight.

81
00:03:48,439 --> 00:03:51,919
All you need to do is get the short arm of the lever under the load

82
00:03:51,919 --> 00:03:53,680
and push down on the long arm.

83
00:03:53,919 --> 00:03:56,639
And the longer the arm, the more weight you can lift.

84
00:03:57,599 --> 00:04:00,879
And that's how a lever makes people stronger!

85
00:04:04,079 --> 00:04:06,639
Well, can we find a fulcrum in here?

86
00:04:06,879 --> 00:04:09,240
Maybe the stumbo. Can that be our fulcrum?

87
00:04:09,319 --> 00:04:10,240
Great idea!

88
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:12,039
Now you're thinking the right way.

89
00:04:14,919 --> 00:04:15,879
You ready to go?

90
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:17,000
Let's go!

91
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,800
Lean on it, Tom Thomas!

92
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:25,879
Yay! It's working!

93
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:28,560
Tideesh!

94
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:30,800
I'm so strong! Did you see?

95
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,720
Now watch how I lift Dad's heavy weights for you.

96
00:04:33,879 --> 00:04:35,800
Look! I can do it!

97
00:04:38,439 --> 00:04:42,120
It's just like I told you! You'd be better off training with my weights!

98
00:04:43,519 --> 00:04:45,519
Didn't you just see me lift up the sofa?

99
00:04:45,519 --> 00:04:47,639
You didn't lift the sofa, the lever did!

100
00:04:47,799 --> 00:04:49,279
Did you ever hear the saying,

101
00:04:49,399 --> 00:04:50,839
knowledge is power?

102
00:04:51,519 --> 00:04:52,519
I've heard it.

103
00:04:52,719 --> 00:04:56,639
Although, some physical power won't hurt you either.

104
00:04:57,719 --> 00:05:00,959
So pick up your lever and go out and play some hockey!

105
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:04,399
You know how built those hockey players are!

